[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572181568","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113121#issuecomment-3572181568","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113121","id":3572181568,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U6ypA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T18:33:15Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T18:35:22Z","body":"The incorrect display is in the FileSystem display? It seems to display correctly otherwise\n\nIt seems that using \"Lossless\" for compression and disabling mipmaps makes it render correctly (though it's using filtering) so it's probably simply an edge case where compression and texture generation causes issues on very small textures\n\nThe \"VRAM Compressed\" and \"Basis Universal\" modes seem to be the common factor","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572181568/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572241430","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113121#issuecomment-3572241430","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113121","id":3572241430,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U7BQW","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T18:50:57Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T18:52:12Z","body":"VRAM-compressed texture formats require textures to be using a multiple of 4 pixels on each axis. If this is not the case, textures will automatically have padding pixels added on one or both axes.\n\nSince using VRAM compression on such small textures will not save any noticeable amount of memory, you should change the compress mode to Lossless for these textures.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/45587 originally disabled VRAM compression for small textures automatically, but it was reverted due to concerns about increasing memory usage for projects that use a lot of 256×256 textures (especially on mobile devices). Maybe we should revisit it, but with a lower size threshold like 16×16 or 32×32.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572241430/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572299096","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113121#issuecomment-3572299096","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113121","id":3572299096,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U7PVY","user":{"login":"miruji","id":147953988,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNGZRA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147953988?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji","html_url":"https://github.com/miruji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T19:07:52Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T19:07:52Z","body":"> VRAM-compressed texture formats require textures to be using a multiple of 4 pixels on each axis. If this is not the case, textures will automatically have padding pixels added on one or both axes.\n> \n> Since using VRAM compression on such small textures will not save any noticeable amount of memory, you should change the compress mode to Lossless for these textures.\n> \n> [#45587](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/45587) originally disabled VRAM compression for small textures automatically, but it was reverted due to concerns about increasing memory usage for projects that use a lot of 256×256 textures (especially on mobile devices). Maybe we should revisit it, but with a lower size threshold like 16×16 or 32×32.\n\nSo, it renders it inside the editor the same way as it was loaded into the project? But then why does it display incorrectly in the project tree or on the material, while in the game itself everything looks fine?  \n\nBut the idea is good—if your suggestion works for small images, it should fix everything. As far as I remember, this error doesn’t occur with 16x16 textures anymore.  \n\nIn any case, it’s not a critical bug, but it can sometimes be confusing during development and is desirable to fix. By the way, in some file managers this is solved using fuzzy thumbnails, like in Thunar on Linux.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572299096/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3576865734","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113121#issuecomment-3576865734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113121","id":3576865734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VMqPG","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T18:01:40Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T18:01:40Z","body":"The issue is that we handle some VRAM textures incorrectly. \n\nDue to how our compressors work, we should resize the images to a multiple-of-4 resolution and operate on that data. We currently only pad the textures without actually resizing them, which works for most cases, but causes some bugs with mipmaps. If I recall correctly we don't even handle 2x2 textures this way, though they still should be resized to 4x4. \n\nAnother issue is how we handle mipmaps in these cases - usually, the resized texture will require an additional 1x1 mipmap which we don't provide, so the last mipmap's color will be set to garbage data in said case. < 4x4 textures will require 2 mipmaps, for 2x2 and 1x1.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3576865734/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3580024370","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113121#issuecomment-3580024370","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113121","id":3580024370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VYtYy","user":{"login":"ghost","id"